    <string name="badges_access_needed_summary">Needed to know which apps have notifications</string>
    <string name="badges_full_build_only">Available in the full version of Haven (from app stores, or the \"-full\" APK). It needs notification access, which Google Play Protect blocks for apps installed from a browser in some countries.</string>
    <string name="badges_disclosure_title">Notification access</string>
    <string name="badges_disclosure_body">Haven uses notification access for two things: a dot or number on app icons, and holding notifications from apps you paused until the pause ends.\n\nHaven only looks at which app each notification is from. It never reads, stores or sends their content, and it has no internet access.\n\nIn the next screen, turn on \"Haven badges and pauses\". If Android says it\'s a restricted setting, open App info for Haven, tap ⋮ and choose \"Allow restricted settings\", then try again.</string>

